Z||000000||Spyder||04-13-2000||01:15 PM||||I need to drop the rear at least 3” for my kit car project.<BR>I have Koni Adjustable Struts already and I want to use them.<BR>I have cut down my Suspension Techniques lowering  springs 3/4 of a coil and I still need a drop of one and a half inches. The springs themselves are getting a little too short for me.<BR>My options are below:<P>Ground Control which cost $199.00: <A HREF="http://www.ground-control.com/gcapguid.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ground-control.com/gcapguid.htm</A> <P>Shelby Customs which cost  $214.00: <A HREF="http://www.shelbycustom.com/r-coil/r-coil.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.shelbycustom.com/r-coil/r-coil.html</A> <P>Ryane Motorsports  which cost $264.00: <A HREF="http://www.ryanemotorsports.com/coilk.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ryanemotorsports.com/coilk.htm</A> <P>Also on another note:<BR> I ordered the Cadillac ball joints to lower the front and they should be in today. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Shiner||04-13-2000||03:38 PM||||Uh, wouldn't a 3" drop be kind of dangerous on a street car?  That would put the car about two inches off the ground standing still.  What happens when you hit a pothole, or run over a big stick in the road?||||reg||4
Z||000002||1FST2M6||04-13-2000||03:58 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.carrerashocks.com" TARGET=_blank>www.carrerashocks.com</A>    they can make you the correct strut rod length and the right coil over spring rate and placement. they have made MANY custom setups for some the cars at Engineered Performance. There is a customer with a 98 Infinity G20 hes racing in the Cup Lite series they made a SWEET set for him.. I would'd try to turn the coilover all the way down with any strut. i've ridden in lots or cars with coil overs, cut springs and various combos they don't handle well don't have proper tire contact patch. Your going to drop some money into a SHARP kit upgrade.. i wouldn't skimp on the suspension. I have Konis and Eibachs.. I could deal with a lower car but I'm pushing the rear arms now... with me in the car they are almost dead level... giving the car FULL suspension travel... There is a point on almost everything of diminishing return... 3" drop would seem to me to be past that point. if you doctor them to much you'll more than likley be dissappointed. May look nice.. but odds are it will not perform as well as it looks. Working at NOPI <A HREF="http://www.nopi.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nopi.com</A>  the year+ that i did gave me a chance to learn what to skimp on and what to do right so you don't kick yourself... suspension is one you don't get cheap on. You do beautiful work and keep a perfect car looking at your site... don't disrupt the performace shearly for astetics.  ||||reg||1
